<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 16:00:16 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>US shows ‘increasingly blatant’ bias over DRC peace deal, says Rwandan minister</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260702-us-shows-increasingly-blatant-bias-over-drc-peace-deal-says-rwandan-fm-olivier-nduhungirehe</link><description>
The fragile peace process between Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of Congo is under renewed pressure, as the United States imposes fresh sanctions over alleged links to mineral trafficking from areas controlled by M23 rebels. Rwandan Foreign Minister Olivier Nduhungirehe tells RFI Kigali is being unfairly blamed – arguing that the Congolese government has failed to meet its own commitments under the US-brokered peace deal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb834410-4076-11f1-9d89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CY3LW.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb834410-4076-11f1-9d89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CY3LW.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8f5ef0c-7617-11f1-bd46-ef6f72536f63</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 15:58:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fb834410-4076-11f1-9d89-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33CY3LW.jpg">© Alexis Huguet / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France issues water safety alert after more than 90 drowning deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-france-issues-water-safety-alert-after-more-than-90-drowning-deaths-heatwave</link><description>
The French government said more than 90 people have died by drowning since 19 June, as authorities and swimming bodies stepped up warnings during a summer marked by intense heat and more people seeking relief in rivers, lakes, canals and pools.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28f3ca9e-7611-11f1-9b77-55a00649bc60</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 15:03:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d9117a0c-7611-11f1-a723-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8CJ2WF.jpg">AFP - ARNAUD FINISTRE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfires spread across southern France, as heatwave reignites forest concerns</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-wildfires-spread-across-southern-france-as-heatwave-reignites-forest-concerns</link><description>
Wildfires have broken out across southern France, forcing evacuations and stretching firefighting teams as the country prepares for the third heatwave of the summer, with the country's forests under increasing threat from climate change and disputes over logging.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76a15890-75f0-11f1-ae1f-a949136140ad</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 13:36:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg">AFP - LIONEL BONAVENTURE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>World Bank drops climate funding target, raising fears for Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260702-world-bank-drops-climate-funding-target-raising-fears-for-africa</link><description>
The World Bank has abandoned its target of directing 45 percent of its financing to projects that help tackle climate change, prompting warnings that poorer countries – especially in Africa – could receive less support to adapt to a warming world.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/16c63082-95a9-11ee-894a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23341508788290.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/16c63082-95a9-11ee-894a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23341508788290.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b91adfd8-7538-11f1-9bc1-c774f26789d8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 10:43:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/16c63082-95a9-11ee-894a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23341508788290.jpg">AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris death penalty congress warns abolition cannot be taken for granted</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-macron-warns-death-penalty-debate-is-back-as-executions-rise-worldwide</link><description>
The fight to abolish the death penalty remains "eminently contemporary", French President Emmanuel Macron said as campaigners, judges and former death row prisoners gathered in Paris this week for the World Congress Against the Death Penalty, amid rising executions worldwide and renewed support for capital punishment in some democracies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f30e478e-7524-11f1-b65e-7129b96364f7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 09:44:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg">ASSOCIATED PRESS - Pat Sullivan</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on France</category><title>Podcast: Adapting to heat, France's fitness boom, Paris Mosque at 100</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-france/20260702-podcast-climate-adaptation-heatwave-fitness-paris-mosque-algeria-france</link><description>
As France's record-breaking heatwave last week raises questions about how the country will have to adapt to a warming climate, we look at what that could mean for French culture. We also explore the country's growing interest in fitness – driven in part by its most popular YouTuber – and examine how the Grand Mosque of Paris, which marks its centenary this year, became both a symbol of Islam in France and a recurring source of political tension.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34686256-760a-11f1-bf8b-a7557f473b29</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 14:30:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sarah Elzas</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Google loses final appeal against EU’s record €4.1bn anti-trust fine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260702-google-loses-final-appeal-against-eu-s-record-%E2%82%AC4-1bn-anti-trust-fine</link><description>
The European Union’s top court has dismissed Google’s final appeal against a record €4.1 billion anti-trust fine, confirming one of Brussels’ most significant victories in its long-running effort to rein in Big Tech.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e56bb90-75ef-11f1-acfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B67G7G6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e56bb90-75ef-11f1-acfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B67G7G6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a78c30fc-75ea-11f1-ad04-cfc389d0d340</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 09:48:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e56bb90-75ef-11f1-acfb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B67G7G6.jpg">AFP - KIRILL KUDRYAVTSEV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Algeria votes in parliamentary elections amid public apathy and football fever</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260702-algeria-votes-in-parliamentary-elections-amid-public-apathy-and-football-fever</link><description>
Algerians are voting in parliamentary elections on Thursday, with cost of living concerns, questions over political freedoms and the national football team’s World Cup run all competing for public attention.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/87002b0c-75e2-11f1-a0e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria2bis.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/87002b0c-75e2-11f1-a0e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria2bis.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">23d54ece-75e0-11f1-b2c6-e7d878263f35</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 07:12:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/87002b0c-75e2-11f1-a0e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria2bis.jpeg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France confirms dates for 2027 presidential election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260701-france-confirms-dates-for-2027-presidential-election-april-may</link><description>
France will hold the first round of its next presidential election on 18 April 2027 and the runoff on 2 May after the government formally approved the dates at Wednesday's cabinet meeting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0669c7d6-754d-11f1-af71-d16dd1da17f0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 14:41:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b483664a-7202-11f1-98b5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36374RG.jpg">© THEO ROUBY / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France advances assisted dying law with strict rules and safeguards</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-france-advances-assisted-dying-law-with-safeguards-and-strict-rules</link><description>
France's National Assembly has approved a new version of a bill creating a legal right to assisted dying, bringing the country closer to a major change in end-of-life care. The legislation sets out who could qualify, how requests would be made and the safeguards designed to prevent abuse of the law. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">859a835a-7558-11f1-8d03-c36d4528ccb7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 06:05:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/494af50a-7559-11f1-ae59-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20122472087525.jpg">AP - Mosa'ab Elshamy</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Senegal squander two-goal lead as Tielemans steals the show for Belgium</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260701-senegal-squander-two-goal-lead-as-tielemans-steals-the-show-for-belgium-world-cup-2026</link><description>
